\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 5. The really important distinction from ordinary mixed Nash\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is where QRE becomes more interesting to someone who already knows game theory.\
A 
\f1\b mixed-strategy Nash equilibrium
\f0\b0  doesn't mean:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "Players make random mistakes."\
It means players are indifferent among the actions in the support.\
For example, if\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P(A)=0.6,P(B)=0.4\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 in a mixed Nash equilibrium, the supported strategies have equal expected payoff.\
QRE doesn't require that.\
You can have\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 EU(A)=10\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 and\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 EU(B)=8\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 yet still have\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P(B)>0.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The probability difference reflects 
\f1\b payoff sensitivity
\f0\b0 , rather than indifference.\
That's why QRE is often described as a model of 
\f1\b bounded rationality / stochastic choice
\f0\b0 , rather than merely another equilibrium refinement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 6. QRE gives you something Nash doesn't\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Suppose the payoff difference between two prices is tiny:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 EU(\'a31.74)=100 EU(\'a31.75)=99.8.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A deterministic Nash model says:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'a31.74 wins. Choose it.\
But empirically, it would be unreasonable to expect firms to behave as though a 20p-per-day difference is infinitely important.\
QRE says:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P(\'a31.74)>P(\'a31.75)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 but perhaps only slightly.\
That's economically meaningful.\
The 
\f1\b magnitude of the payoff difference matters
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 7. Interpretation of \uc0\u955 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is where I would be careful with the term 
\f2\i rationality
\f0\i0 .\
Mathematically, \uc0\u955  is a 
\f1\b precision parameter
\f0\b0 .\
Consider two prices with expected profits:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 U1 =100,U2 =95.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Then\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P2 P1 =e\uc0\u955 (U1 \u8722 U2 )=e5\u955 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Therefore:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Low \uc0\u955 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u955 =0.1\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 gives\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P2 P1 =e0.5\uc0\u8776 1.65.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Only modest preference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 High \uc0\u955 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \uc0\u955 =1\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 gives\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P2 P1 =e5\uc0\u8776 148.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Almost deterministic.\
So \uc0\u955  controls 
\f1\b how strongly payoff differences translate into choice probabilities
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 8. Connection to discrete choice\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Given your pricing background, this is probably the most useful mental model:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Logit demand\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 You may already have something like\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P(j)=\uc0\u8721 k eVk eVj\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 where consumers choose products probabilistically according to utility.\
QRE essentially applies the same mathematical machinery to 
\f1\b strategic players
\f0\b0 .\
Instead of:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Vj =consumer\'a0utility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 you have:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Vj =EUi (j,\uc0\u963 \u8722 i )\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'97the expected payoff to the strategic player.\
So:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 QRE is essentially a logit response model embedded inside a game.
\f0\b0 \
