\cf0 As:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \uc0\u955 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 \uc0\u8734 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 you get:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 P(p
\f3 \uc0\u8727 
\f0 )
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 1.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So yes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 QRE\uc0\u955 
\f5 \uc0\u8594 
\f0 \uc0\u8734  Nash\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 in the appropriate sense.\
Therefore, if your only criterion is 
\f1\b profit maximisation under a known payoff model
