\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 6. But there's an even more interesting problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Increasing \uc0\u955  isn't necessarily "becoming more rational."\
That's an interpretation we often attach to the parameter.\
Mathematically, you're saying:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "Small payoff differences have a weak effect on choice."\
versus\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "Small payoff differences have a strong effect on choice."\
Consider:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 EU(p1 )=100.0 EU(p2 )=99.9.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 At high \uc0\u955 , you effectively say:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 "A 10p difference makes the firm overwhelmingly choose p1 ."\
But a real pricing organisation might have a much bigger source of uncertainty than 10p of expected profit.\
So 
\f1\b high \uc0\u955  isn't necessarily more realistic.
\f0\b0 \
It is only more consistent with the assumption that firms respond very precisely to payoff differences.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 7. There's also an important distinction between QRE and "randomising"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is often misunderstood.\
A QRE does 
\f1\b not necessarily mean the manager wakes up every morning and flips a weighted coin.
\f0\b0 \
You can interpret the logit formulation as arising from a latent payoff:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 U~i (p)=EUi (p)+
\f5 \uc0\u1013 
\f0 ip\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 where 
\f5 \uc0\u1013 
\f0 ip represents unobserved payoff/decision noise.\
The firm chooses:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 pi =argpmax [EUi (p)+
\f5 \uc0\u1013 
\f0 ip ].\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 If the 
\f5 \uc0\u1013 
\f0 's have the appropriate extreme-value distribution, you get the logit QRE probabilities.\
Now the probability has a much more natural interpretation.\
The firm 
\f1\b still chooses one price
\f0\b0 .\
We\'97the modeller\'97don't observe the firm's complete latent decision environment.\
Hence we predict a probability distribution.\
That is much more defensible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 8. Now let's turn your argument around\
