\f0\fs24 \cf0 And 
\f1\b MaxEnt sits underneath the QRE response mechanism
\f0\b0 , not as an alternative to demand modelling.\
So I'd sharpen the earlier debate considerably:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Demand modelling tells you what the economic consequences of a price are. Nash tells you how a perfectly strategic firm responds to those consequences. QRE tells you how a strategically interacting firm responds when the mapping from payoff to action is probabilistic/entropy-regularised.
\f0\b0 \
And your observation that 
\f1\b logit QRE is essentially an entropy-regularised best response
\f0\b0  is exactly the bridge between the game-theory and MaxEnt perspectives.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
